WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.490
- All right, welcome back.

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:03.597
Our next guest stars in
the hit show Riverdale.

00:00:03.597 --> 00:00:06.660
And you can see it on
the CW and on Netflix.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.374
Let's say hello to
Charles Melton everybody.

00:00:09.374 --> 00:00:13.890
(audience applauds)
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.390
Hello, it's lovely to meet you.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.680
- Lovely to meet you too, Kelly.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.290
- Yes, well congrats on
all the success, man.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:23.810
Riverdale is so massive and
you have a huge fan base.

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:26.750
What's your craziest
experience with a fan?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.800
- Craziest experience.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.843
I'd probably say the time a fan

00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:36.843
came up to me and she asked
me to write love is love.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.940
And I, for some reason I misspelled love

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.170
but she was gonna get
a tattoo on her wrist.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.000
And I was like, "I'm so sorry,"

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.870
and she's like, "No, no,
no, I'm gonna keep it."

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.450
So I haven't seen it today, but I'm sure,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.000
if you see someone that has love is love

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.530
with the love crossed out,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:57.630
that's probably, that's my artwork.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.463
- Oh my God.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:00.290
Wait, so wait, you ended
up crossing out the love.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:01.800
Now, it got cool.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.130
So love is dark.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.500
It's a dark tattoo, mind you.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.123
But I think it's cool.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.953
- Thank you.

00:01:07.953 --> 00:01:09.523
Yeah, I crossed it out and rewrote it

00:01:09.523 --> 00:01:11.280
and she was like, "I'm gonna keep it,"

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.280
and I was like, "Okay, cool, awesome."

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.140
- I get so nervous when people do that

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.190
they asked me to do lyrics and they're,

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.430
and I don't know why I'm doing it.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.640
And then they're like, "I'm
gonna get it tattooed,"

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.067
And I'm like, "I can't express to you

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.607
"how bad of an idea that is actually.

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:24.810
"Like you shouldn't do that."

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.930
I was like, "You might hate me one day."

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.560
I'm just saying like, it could be like

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.633
she sucks and it's there.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:32.880
- It's so much pressure.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.180
'Cause I'm like, all right
now it's, do I do cursive?

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.740
Do I do block letters?

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.590
What do I do?

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.400
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.330
- Well, I hear that you
love the Food Channel.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:42.690
So do you cook?

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:43.830
- I do cook.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.642
I try to cook every meal.

00:01:45.642 --> 00:01:48.200
- Oh, what's your favorite thing to cook?

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:53.200
- I like to cook a grilled
peanut butter and jelly sandwich.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.520
- Yes.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.690
Crunchy peanut butter or creamy?

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.283
- Oh, it's, it depends.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.690
It's crispy on the outside.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:05.490
It's like a grilled cheese,
you know, I layer the butter,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:10.010
sourdough bread, layer the
peanut butter, the jelly

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:13.900
and I just grill it and it is heaven.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.128
I had three last night.

00:02:15.128 --> 00:02:16.720
- Three, oh my God.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.310
I want your metabolism.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:20.160
Okay, so, I want that sandwich too,

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.000
it sounds amazing.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.690
I'm crunchy all the way by the way.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:25.380
But you recently published an essay

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.140
about the rise in anti-Asian hate crimes.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:27.973
And I think this is so important

00:02:27.973 --> 00:02:29.690
because you have a huge spotlight on you.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.682
Why was it important to you?

00:02:31.682 --> 00:02:35.530
- I felt that it was
important to share my story.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.590
My experience.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:40.890
And you know, I've always
had this push and pull

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:44.350
between whether I was Asian enough,

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:45.210
or white enough,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.360
or American enough.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.970
You know, I describe it as
two cars being cut in half

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.440
and attached together in the middle,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.760
one side being Korean,

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.780
the other side being American.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.500
And just depending on the day

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.570
I would assimilate with one or the other.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.370
And I just realized that my experience is

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:07.200
an Asian American story,
an American story.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.310
And I just felt the,
the need to share that.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.240
- Well, I think it's really important.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:14.910
What steps do you think

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.240
that people can take to
help the AAPI community?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.280
- I think a step everyone can take

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.280
is just recognizing Asian American,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.790
the Asian American experience,

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.560
as a part of American history and culture.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.580
As far as the Chinese Exclusion Act,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.750
Japanese interment camps

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.140
just understanding the history.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:35.610
The Asian American history
that our countries have.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.830
- Yeah, I think it's important too,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.000
like in school, I remember
in school growing up

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.520
I only learned that these certain things

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.330
in history and I think
it's really important,

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.330
I think now it's a little more progressive

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.560
in all areas of the country,

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.470
but I think more progression is needed.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.880
But to really, that's
where, when you're a kid

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.740
you start learning about
all these different cultures

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.330
all these different, these people that,

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.110
and that's the coolest thing about America

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.540
is we're this giant melting pot of all,

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.640
I mean, all our people are
from somewhere else, you know?

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.610
So it's an amazing thing.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.670
I think they should really
start incorporating in schools

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.140
but I love that you did the essay.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.130
I think it's very important.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.140
And I also think another thing that's cool

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:09.980
that you're doing

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.900
you're also a global ambassador
for the Special Olympics.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.290
So why is that important to you?

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:18.580
- You know, I grew up
a, I'm a former athlete.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.670
I played football at
Kansas State University

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.810
and being a military brat
every two to four years

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.480
I was moving to a different
place around the world

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.480
and I found a sense of community
and identity in sports.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.570
So my love for sports,
mixed with my love for kids

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:38.300
and finding Special Olympics

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:42.410
and how they encourage inclusivity

00:04:43.752 --> 00:04:45.082
and being a part of that

00:04:45.082 --> 00:04:49.860
has been a special place in my heart to,

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.754
you know, bring awareness
to Special Olympics

00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:54.337
and inclusivity to,

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.950
through my social media
platform, Instagram.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.173
- Absolutely, that's what I always say.

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:00.006
It's so cool.

00:05:00.006 --> 00:05:01.790
Like, we're blessed with
the spotlight, but it's,

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.960
it's a bigger blessing
to bless others with it.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.460
So it's really cool
thing that you're doing

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.360
and it is lovely to meet you Charles.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.193
(audience applauds)

00:05:08.193 --> 00:05:09.480
- Thanks Kelly, lovely to meet you too.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.576
I'm a huge fan by the way.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.680
- Oh, thank you.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.430
Even if you're lying, I'll take it.

00:05:14.873 --> 00:05:16.063
I'm totally messing with you

00:05:17.747 --> 00:05:19.254
- I'm a huge fan.

00:05:19.254 --> 00:05:21.140
- I'm a huge fan of your peanut butter

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.953
and jelly sandwich that I now want.

00:05:24.043 --> 00:05:26.260
Well, I am a huge fan of your work too

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:28.260
so you have to come back
to the show, all right?

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.180
- I've love that, thank you.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.370
- All right, well, everybody be sure

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.753
to check out Riverdale
on the CW and Netflix.

